{"encoding": "verislop.autonomous-critique/0.1", "phase": "formalize", "attempt": 1, "request": "Software engineering task G03: Negative-cycle propagation in shortest paths\n\nImplement solution.py with solve(data). Use only the Python standard library. Do not read files, use the network, print, or retain state across calls. All inputs conform to this specification; return JSON-compatible values. Input {n,source,edges}, n=1..10, edges [u,v,cost] with integer cost -6..9. Return a length-n distance list from source. Unreachable vertices are null. A vertex reachable from a negative-cost cycle that is itself reachable from source is \"-inf\". Other vertices have their minimum integer walk cost; source starts at distance zero. Parallel edges and self-loops are allowed; an unreachable negative cycle must not affect output.\n\nImplement a pure deterministic Python 3 function solve(data) in solution.py. Use only the standard library, no external I/O. The function receives a JSON value and returns a JSON-serializable value. Preserve the specified input/output structure and exact ordering.\n\nPublic examples (additional held-out cases will be scored):\n[{\"input\": {\"edges\": [[0, 1, 2], [1, 2, -3], [2, 1, 1], [2, 3, 4], [4, 4, -1]], \"n\": 5, \"source\": 0}, \"output\": [0, \"-inf\", \"-inf\", \"-inf\", null]}, {\"input\": {\"edges\": [[1, 1, -1]], \"n\": 3, \"source\": 0}, \"output\": [0, null, null]}]\n", "clauses": [{"clause_id": "C1", "quote": "Software engineering task G03: Negative-cycle propagation in shortest paths", "refs": []}, {"clause_id": "C2", "quote": "Implement solution.py with solve(data).", "refs": ["O1"]}, {"clause_id": "C3", "quote": "Use only the Python standard library.", "refs": ["R1"]}, {"clause_id": "C4", "quote": "Do not read files, use the network, print, or retain state across calls.", "refs": ["S2"]}, {"clause_id": "C5", "quote": "All inputs conform to this specification;", "refs": ["A1"]}, {"clause_id": "C6", "quote": "return JSON-compatible values.", "refs": ["O1"]}, {"clause_id": "C7", "quote": "Input {n,source,edges}, n=1..10, edges [u,v,cost] with integer cost -6..9.", "refs": ["D1"]}, {"clause_id": "C8", "quote": "Return a length-n distance list from source.", "refs": ["O1"]}, {"clause_id": "C9", "quote": "Unreachable vertices are null.", "refs": ["O2"]}, {"clause_id": "C10", "quote": "A vertex reachable from a negative-cost cycle that is itself reachable from source is \"-inf\".", "refs": ["O3"]}, {"clause_id": "C11", "quote": "Other vertices have their minimum integer walk cost;", "refs": ["O4"]}, {"clause_id": "C12", "quote": "source starts at distance zero.", "refs": ["O4"]}, {"clause_id": "C13", "quote": "Parallel edges and self-loops are allowed;", "refs": ["D1"]}, {"clause_id": "C14", "quote": "an unreachable negative cycle must not affect output.", "refs": ["S1"]}, {"clause_id": "C15", "quote": "Implement a pure deterministic Python 3 function solve(data) in solution.py.", "refs": ["O1", "S2"]}, {"clause_id": "C16", "quote": "Use only the standard library, no external I/O.", "refs": ["R1", "S2"]}, {"clause_id": "C17", "quote": "The function receives a JSON value and returns a JSON-serializable value.", "refs": ["O1"]}, {"clause_id": "C18", "quote": "Preserve the specified input/output structure and exact ordering.", "refs": ["O1"]}, {"clause_id": "C19", "quote": "Public examples (additional held-out cases will be scored):\n[{\"input\": {\"edges\": [[0, 1, 2], [1, 2, -3], [2, 1, 1], [2, 3, 4], [4, 4, -1]], \"n\": 5, \"source\": 0}, \"output\": [0, \"-inf\", \"-inf\", \"-inf\", null]}, {\"input\": {\"edges\": [[1, 1, -1]], \"n\": 3, \"source\": 0}, \"output\": [0, null, null]}]", "refs": ["O5"]}], "records": [{"id": "D1", "revision": 1, "kind": "entity", "role": "declaration", "statement": "Input is a JSON object with n, source, and edges; n is 1 through 10, and each directed edge [u,v,cost] has integer cost from -6 through 9. Parallel edges and self-loops are supported.", "required": true, "source_refs": [{"document_hash": "sha256:4fdd2d671c8824e8de9e97f49948b9099777fbc4c9268e84b28d4f84b5ce8811", "document_ref": "tasks/G03/prompt.txt", "end_byte": 375, "interpretation": "Graph input domain.", "origin": "explicit", "start_byte": 301}, {"document_hash": "sha256:4fdd2d671c8824e8de9e97f49948b9099777fbc4c9268e84b28d4f84b5ce8811", "document_ref": "tasks/G03/prompt.txt", "end_byte": 673, "interpretation": "Permitted edge configurations.", "origin": "explicit", "start_byte": 631}], "scope": ["input graph"], "dependencies": [], "acceptance_criteria": ["Accept the specified graph representation, including parallel edges and self-loops."], "origin": "interpreted", "record_digest": "sha256:7ffe7fcbf297ce2537f2ecc99123ee3b82542eb09b53fc4d13734fd158df0c27", "blocked_by": []}, {"id": "A1", "revision": 1, "kind": "precondition", "role": "assumption", "statement": "Inputs conform to the specification.", "required": true, "source_refs": [{"document_hash": "sha256:4fdd2d671c8824e8de9e97f49948b9099777fbc4c9268e84b28d4f84b5ce8811", "document_ref": "tasks/G03/prompt.txt", "end_byte": 269, "interpretation": "Explicit input conformity assumption.", "origin": "explicit", "start_byte": 228}], "scope": ["all invocations"], "dependencies": [{"id": "D1", "relation": "uses_definition"}], "acceptance_criteria": ["The caller supplies a conforming input."], "origin": "interpreted", "record_digest": "sha256:877864847ae005f899fef65251e923c801f438a5c5356c02e501e06add983e8a", "blocked_by": []}, {"id": "O1", "revision": 1, "kind": "postcondition", "role": "guarantee", "statement": "Provide a Python 3 function solve(data) in solution.py receiving the specified JSON value and returning a JSON-serializable length-n list, ordered by vertex index, with distances from source.", "required": true, "source_refs": [{"document_hash": "sha256:4fdd2d671c8824e8de9e97f49948b9099777fbc4c9268e84b28d4f84b5ce8811", "document_ref": "tasks/G03/prompt.txt", "end_byte": 116, "interpretation": "Required file and entry point.", "origin": "explicit", "start_byte": 77}, {"document_hash": "sha256:4fdd2d671c8824e8de9e97f49948b9099777fbc4c9268e84b28d4f84b5ce8811", "document_ref": "tasks/G03/prompt.txt", "end_byte": 420, "interpretation": "Output shape and meaning.", "origin": "explicit", "start_byte": 376}, {"document_hash": "sha256:4fdd2d671c8824e8de9e97f49948b9099777fbc4c9268e84b28d4f84b5ce8811", "document_ref": "tasks/G03/prompt.txt", "end_byte": 300, "interpretation": "Output serialization.", "origin": "explicit", "start_byte": 270}, {"document_hash": "sha256:4fdd2d671c8824e8de9e97f49948b9099777fbc4c9268e84b28d4f84b5ce8811", "document_ref": "tasks/G03/prompt.txt", "end_byte": 927, "interpretation": "JSON interface.", "origin": "explicit", "start_byte": 854}, {"document_hash": "sha256:4fdd2d671c8824e8de9e97f49948b9099777fbc4c9268e84b28d4f84b5ce8811", "document_ref": "tasks/G03/prompt.txt", "end_byte": 993, "interpretation": "Vertex-index ordering and structure.", "origin": "explicit", "start_byte": 928}, {"document_hash": "sha256:4fdd2d671c8824e8de9e97f49948b9099777fbc4c9268e84b28d4f84b5ce8811", "document_ref": "tasks/G03/prompt.txt", "end_byte": 805, "interpretation": "Python version and interface.", "origin": "explicit", "start_byte": 729}], "scope": ["function interface and output"], "dependencies": [{"id": "D1", "relation": "uses_definition"}, {"id": "A1", "relation": "assumes"}], "acceptance_criteria": ["solution.py exposes solve(data).", "The output is JSON-serializable and has exactly n entries.", "Entry v corresponds to vertex v and preserves the specified structure and ordering."], "origin": "interpreted", "record_digest": "sha256:71050ca85768d2388e6fe1677693893ff85df8f119b5fa96a9fae7c6e95aa821", "blocked_by": []}, {"id": "O2", "revision": 1, "kind": "postcondition", "role": "guarantee", "statement": "Every vertex unreachable from source has output null.", "required": true, "source_refs": [{"document_hash": "sha256:4fdd2d671c8824e8de9e97f49948b9099777fbc4c9268e84b28d4f84b5ce8811", "document_ref": "tasks/G03/prompt.txt", "end_byte": 451, "interpretation": "Unreachable distance representation.", "origin": "explicit", "start_byte": 421}], "scope": ["unreachable vertices"], "dependencies": [{"id": "D1", "relation": "uses_definition"}, {"id": "A1", "relation": "assumes"}], "acceptance_criteria": ["For every vertex with no directed walk from source, its output entry is null."], "origin": "interpreted", "record_digest": "sha256:3e28d81de09e3531d283c2128588a07e1843644a3c1cf41cea5beb6afcca300f", "blocked_by": []}, {"id": "O3", "revision": 1, "kind": "postcondition", "role": "guarantee", "statement": "Every vertex reachable from a negative-cost cycle reachable from source has output string \"-inf\".", "required": true, "source_refs": [{"document_hash": "sha256:4fdd2d671c8824e8de9e97f49948b9099777fbc4c9268e84b28d4f84b5ce8811", "document_ref": "tasks/G03/prompt.txt", "end_byte": 545, "interpretation": "Negative-cycle propagation.", "origin": "explicit", "start_byte": 452}], "scope": ["vertices downstream of source-reachable negative cycles"], "dependencies": [{"id": "D1", "relation": "uses_definition"}, {"id": "A1", "relation": "assumes"}], "acceptance_criteria": ["Mark cycle vertices and all vertices reachable from them as \"-inf\" whenever the cycle is reachable from source.", "This rule also applies to source if such a cycle can reach source."], "origin": "interpreted", "record_digest": "sha256:8e83f030c458d9aef84314a5c8f2d1e4cfe800b80112000d99196abda3463e1c", "blocked_by": []}, {"id": "O4", "revision": 1, "kind": "postcondition", "role": "guarantee", "statement": "For each reachable vertex outside negative-cycle propagation, return its minimum integer walk cost from source, using zero as the cost of the initial empty walk at source.", "required": true, "source_refs": [{"document_hash": "sha256:4fdd2d671c8824e8de9e97f49948b9099777fbc4c9268e84b28d4f84b5ce8811", "document_ref": "tasks/G03/prompt.txt", "end_byte": 598, "interpretation": "Finite shortest-walk semantics.", "origin": "explicit", "start_byte": 546}, {"document_hash": "sha256:4fdd2d671c8824e8de9e97f49948b9099777fbc4c9268e84b28d4f84b5ce8811", "document_ref": "tasks/G03/prompt.txt", "end_byte": 630, "interpretation": "Initial empty-walk cost.", "origin": "explicit", "start_byte": 599}], "scope": ["finite distances"], "dependencies": [{"id": "D1", "relation": "uses_definition"}, {"id": "A1", "relation": "assumes"}], "acceptance_criteria": ["Each finite output equals the minimum cost over directed walks from source.", "The initial source distance is zero; negative-cycle propagation takes precedence when applicable."], "origin": "interpreted", "record_digest": "sha256:b7017b42c93b4c5ce9181d0bf56879a97a131ff29cb37836ec799e828e561f3e", "blocked_by": []}, {"id": "O5", "revision": 1, "kind": "postcondition", "role": "guarantee", "statement": "The supplied public examples produce their exact listed outputs.", "required": true, "source_refs": [{"document_hash": "sha256:4fdd2d671c8824e8de9e97f49948b9099777fbc4c9268e84b28d4f84b5ce8811", "document_ref": "tasks/G03/prompt.txt", "end_byte": 1286, "interpretation": "Required example behavior; held-out scoring supplies evaluation context.", "origin": "explicit", "start_byte": 995}], "scope": ["public examples"], "dependencies": [{"id": "O2", "relation": "uses_proof"}, {"id": "O3", "relation": "uses_proof"}, {"id": "O4", "relation": "uses_proof"}, {"id": "S1", "relation": "uses_proof"}], "acceptance_criteria": ["For n=5, source=0, edges=[[0,1,2],[1,2,-3],[2,1,1],[2,3,4],[4,4,-1]], return [0,\"-inf\",\"-inf\",\"-inf\",null].", "For n=3, source=0, edges=[[1,1,-1]], return [0,null,null]."], "origin": "interpreted", "record_digest": "sha256:001a1efc7871e57b9b6b4fd04db00fc80361998f1b669079486bddc0b0b2824e", "blocked_by": []}, {"id": "S1", "revision": 1, "kind": "safety_property", "role": "guarantee", "statement": "Negative cycles unreachable from source do not affect the output.", "required": true, "source_refs": [{"document_hash": "sha256:4fdd2d671c8824e8de9e97f49948b9099777fbc4c9268e84b28d4f84b5ce8811", "document_ref": "tasks/G03/prompt.txt", "end_byte": 727, "interpretation": "Reachability boundary for negative-cycle effects.", "origin": "explicit", "start_byte": 674}], "scope": ["unreachable negative cycles"], "dependencies": [{"id": "D1", "relation": "uses_definition"}, {"id": "A1", "relation": "assumes"}], "acceptance_criteria": ["An unreachable negative cycle cannot cause any vertex to be marked \"-inf\" or change any distance."], "origin": "interpreted", "record_digest": "sha256:4256f35b49fc84ea0f4b758bf541d6c55fc6ebf45773c4ddd02fea2609fb05e1", "blocked_by": []}, {"id": "S2", "revision": 1, "kind": "safety_property", "role": "guarantee", "statement": "solve is pure and deterministic, performs no external I/O, reads no files, uses no network, prints nothing, and retains no state across calls.", "required": true, "source_refs": [{"document_hash": "sha256:4fdd2d671c8824e8de9e97f49948b9099777fbc4c9268e84b28d4f84b5ce8811", "document_ref": "tasks/G03/prompt.txt", "end_byte": 227, "interpretation": "Prohibited effects and persistent state.", "origin": "explicit", "start_byte": 155}, {"document_hash": "sha256:4fdd2d671c8824e8de9e97f49948b9099777fbc4c9268e84b28d4f84b5ce8811", "document_ref": "tasks/G03/prompt.txt", "end_byte": 805, "interpretation": "Purity and determinism.", "origin": "explicit", "start_byte": 729}, {"document_hash": "sha256:4fdd2d671c8824e8de9e97f49948b9099777fbc4c9268e84b28d4f84b5ce8811", "document_ref": "tasks/G03/prompt.txt", "end_byte": 853, "interpretation": "External I/O prohibition.", "origin": "explicit", "start_byte": 806}], "scope": ["all invocations"], "dependencies": [], "acceptance_criteria": ["Equal inputs yield equal outputs independently of call history.", "No file reads, network operations, printing, external I/O, or retained cross-call state occur.", "Calling solve has no externally observable side effects."], "origin": "interpreted", "reco